# Updating from the Template

This project was generated from the [{{ parent_template_name }}]({{ parent_template_url }})
[Copier](https://copier.readthedocs.io/) template. To pull in its latest changes:

1. Start from a clean working tree on a new branch; Copier refuses to update with
   uncommitted changes.
2. Run `mise run copier-update`. Your recorded answers are reused, so you're only
   asked about questions added since your last update.
3. Resolve any conflicts where your own edits overlap a template change; Copier marks
   them inline.
4. Review any new files in `.changeset/` (one per relevant upstream change) and delete
   the ones that don't apply to your project. Each entry links back to the upstream {{ 'PR' if using_github else 'repo' }} it came
   from, so you can check the source before deciding.
5. Commit and open a pull request as usual. The remaining changes described by files in `.changeset/` are folded into
   your [next release](releasing.md) alongside your own commits.
